    "title": "AMBER Alert canceled after missing girl found safe - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Kevin S. Held ,\n3 hours ago\nST. LOUIS COUNTY, Mo. – The Missouri State Highway Patrol has rescinded its AMBER Alert after an abducted child was found safe in St. Louis County.\nThe alert came down just after 8 p.m. Wednesday.\nThe abduction happened around 1 p.m. at an apartment complex in the 1400 block of Shadycreek Court.\nClose Thanks for signing up!\nWatch for us in your inbox.\nSubscribe Now\nBreaking News Munyaradzi Chiturumani St. Louis County Police said an 8-year-old girl was abducted by her noncustodial father, Munyaradzi Chiturumani.\nPolice said Chiturumanistabbed the girl’s mother before taking the child. Chiturumani has allegedly made threats toward the child.\nChiturumani weighs approximately 165 pounds and stands 5’8″ tall, with brown eyes and black hair.\nChiturumani’s vehicle, a dark blue 2017 Ford Edge, was located unoccupied in the Frontenac area.\nThe alert was canceled after 10 p.m. after the girl was found.\nCopyright 2026 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved. This material may not be published, broadcast, rewritten, or redistributed. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to FOX 2.",
    "summary": "– The Missouri State Highway Patrol has rescinded its AMBER Alert after an abducted child was found safe in St. Louis County. The abduction happened around 1 p.m. at an apartment complex in the 1400 block of Shadycreek Court. Chiturumani weighs approximately 165 pounds and stands 5’8″ tall, with brown eyes and black hair. Chiturumani’s vehicle, a dark blue 2017 Ford Edge, was located unoccupied in the Frontenac area. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to FOX 2.",
